Feature: Leaderboard
  1. Functional Test Cases
       TC-01: Fetch leaderboard successfully
          Steps:
              Open leaderboard screen
              Wait for data to load
          Expected Result:
              List of users with scores is displayed
          Status: PASS
       TC-02: Display correct user data
          Steps:
              Open leaderboard
              Check username and score
          Expected Result:
              Data matches backend response
          Status: PASS
       TC-03: Loading state
          Steps:
               Open leaderboard screen
          Expected Result:
               Loading indicator appears before data loads
          Status: PASS
 2. Error Test Cases
       TC-04: Network failure
          Steps:
               Turn off internet
               Open leaderboard
          Expected Result:
               Error message appears
          Status: PASS
       TC-05: API failure
          Steps:
               Simulate server error
               Fetch leaderboard
          Expected Result:
               Error state is shown
          Status: PASS
 3. Edge Cases
       TC-06: Empty leaderboard
          Steps:
              API returns empty list
         Expected Result:
              Empty state UI is shown (No users found)
         Status: PASS
       TC-07: Large number of users
         Steps:
              Fetch leaderboard with many users
         Expected Result:
              List scrolls correctly without UI issues
         Status: PASS
       TC-08: Data refresh
         Steps:
              Open leaderboard
              Refresh screen (reload)
         Expected Result:
               Updated data is displayed
         Status: PASS
Notes
  * Data is fetched from backend using API
  * No frontend sorting applied (data comes sorted from server)
  * Errors handled using LeaderboardError state
  * Success handled using LeaderboardSuccess state
  * Loading handled using LeaderboardLoading